  "full_text": "They can't be told, my freedom I hold dear. How years ago and days of old, when magic filled the air. Just in the darkest depths of murder, I met a girl so fair. But Gollum, the evil one, crept up and slipped away with her. Away with her. Ramble on. On my way. Been this way ten years to the day. Gotta ramble on. Find the queen of all my dreams. Got no time for spreading roots. Time has come to be gone. Just in the darkest depths of mortar, I met a girl so fair. Ramblin' on. Ramblin' on. Find the queen of all my dreams. How about it? Yeah. You ever heard Hefk by Fastway? I don't think I can sing it. That's a pretty cool song. That's one of my favorite songs. Heft by Fastway is one of my favorite songs. When I was like, I don't know, 13 or something, my brother Danny gave me a bunch of cassette tapes. It had Fastway, it had... Quiet Riot, it had Motley Crue, Too Fast for Love. It had Ozzy Osbourne, Diver, Madman. It had, what else did it have? I think it might have had another Ozzy, and that was like in Michigan. It was a good time. Some of the best music comes from that 13-year-old and a group of tapes or something. Danny probably thinks I'm crazy. Why do you like all that old music? Get new music. I like, Red Fang is the only new music I know of that's good. Red Fang is good. At least the videos are good with the music. Sometimes the music doesn't really stand on its own quite as much. But it's good music. It's good music.",
